<main class="detail-page"><a class="back-link" href="cars.html">← Back to the cars</a><section class="detail-hero image-amg"><div class="detail-title"><p class="eyebrow">MERCEDES-AMG · W205 · 2021 MODEL YEAR</p><h1>C 63 <span>S</span></h1><p>A compact saloon with unmistakable V8 character.</p></div></section>
<section class="detail-intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE STORY</p><h2>Hand-built heart.<br>Rear-drive attitude.</h2></div><div><p>The 2021 C 63 S is the high-performance version of Mercedes-Benz’s W205 C-Class saloon. Under the long bonnet sits AMG’s hand-built 4.0-litre V8 with two turbochargers mounted in the engine’s “hot V”. The S version adds output over the standard C 63 and pairs a quick-shifting AMG SPEEDSHIFT MCT transmission with rear-wheel drive.</p><p>It mixes a comfortable, well-equipped cabin with a playful, powerful personality. Its smaller footprint and rear-drive layout make it feel different from the larger, all-wheel-drive M5 CS.</p></div></section>
<section class="spec-section"><p class="eyebrow">KEY FIGURES · US SEDAN SPECIFICATION</p><h2>At a glance</h2><div class="spec-grid"><div class="spec"><strong>4.0L V8</strong><span>Hand-built biturbo petrol</span></div><div class="spec"><strong>503 hp</strong><span>375 kW at 5,500–6,250 rpm</span></div><div class="spec"><strong>516 lb-ft</strong><span>700 Nm peak torque</span></div><div class="spec"><strong>3.7–3.9 sec</strong><span>0–60 mph, depending on source/test</span></div><div class="spec"><strong>180 mph</strong><span>Manufacturer-quoted top speed</span></div><div class="spec"><strong>9-speed</strong><span>AMG SPEEDSHIFT MCT automatic</span></div><div class="spec"><strong>Rear-wheel drive</strong><span>AMG rear-axle layout</span></div><div class="spec"><strong>$76,200</strong><span>Original US sedan MSRP</span></div></div></section>
<section class="detail-copy"><h2>What makes it special?</h2><div class="copy-grid"><article><h3>AMG V8 soundtrack</h3><p>The 4.0-litre biturbo V8 makes 503 hp and 516 lb-ft in C 63 S form. Its broad torque gives strong acceleration without needing to chase the redline, and the exhaust note is a defining part of the car’s character.</p></article><article><h3>Rear-wheel-drive balance</h3><p>Unlike the M5 CS, the C 63 S sends its power to the rear wheels. The result is a more traditional performance-saloon feel, with selectable drive settings and an electronically controlled rear differential on the S.</p></article><article><h3>Fast, usable saloon</h3><p>Four doors, a proper rear bench, and Mercedes-Benz comfort make the C 63 S usable beyond a weekend drive. AMG performance hardware and a configurable driving character give it a more intense side when the road opens up.</p></article><article><h3>Price note</h3><p>$76,200 was the original US MSRP for the 2021 C 63 S Sedan. It is not a current used price; used values vary substantially with mileage, condition, options, and location.</p></article></div></section>
